<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johan Adolf Pengel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1916">1916</a>–<a href="/years/1970">1970</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Jopie Pengel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johan Adolf Pengel was a Surinamese politician who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-party-of-suriname">National Party of Suriname</a> (NPS), the main party of the Afro-Surinamese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">Creole</a> population. He was prime minister from 1963 to 1969, governing in coalition with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagernath-lachmon">Jagernath Lachmon</a>'s Hindustani party, a partnership known as the politics of fraternisation. His government fell in 1969 after strikes by teachers and other workers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johan-adolf-pengel.jpg" alt="Johan Adolf Pengel" width="320" height="452" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jack de Nijs for Anefo / Anefo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Minister-President_Pengel_profil_1963_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
